    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nWhen trying to use ctrl+d or ctrl+u to scroll half of the page, it scrolls to the current position.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-845+gfacbb11e0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim .`\r\n2. Try to use CTRL+d og CTRL+u\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nTo scroll half of the page up / down.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nIt jumps up, then scrolls to the initial postition of your cursor.\r\n\r\nHere is my configuration.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n\t\t\t-- don't use animate when scrolling with the mouse\r\n\t\t\tlocal mouse_scrolled = false\r\n\t\t\tfor _, scroll in ipairs({ \"Up\", \"Down\" }) do\r\n\t\t\t\tlocal key = \"<ScrollWheel\" .. scroll .. \">\"\r\n\t\t\t\tvim.keymap.set({ \"\", \"i\" }, key, function()\r\n\t\t\t\t\tmouse_scrolled = true\r\n\t\t\t\t\treturn key\r\n\t\t\t\tend, { expr = true })\r\n\t\t\tend\r\n\r\n\t\t\tlocal animate = require(\"mini.animate\")\r\n\t\t\treturn {\r\n\t\t\t\tresize = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\ttiming = animate.gen_timing.linear({ duration = 100, unit = \"total\" }),\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t\tscroll = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\ttiming = animate.gen_timing.linear({ duration = 150, unit = \"total\" }),\r\n\t\t\t\t\tsubscroll = animate.gen_subscroll.equal({\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tpredicate = function(total_scroll)\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif mouse_scrolled then\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmouse_scrolled = false\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn false\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tend\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn total_scroll > 1\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tend,\r\n\t\t\t\t\t}),\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t\topen = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tenable = false\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\tclose = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tenable = false\r\n\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\tend,\r\n\t\tconfig = function(_, opts)\r\n\t\t\trequire(\"mini.animate\").setup(opts)\r\n\t\tend,\r\n```",
